cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SODA, please cite it as below. A paper is in preparation; this entry will point to it once it is published."
type: software
title: "SODA: Spatial Omics Data Annex"
version: 0.9.0
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
authors:
  - family-names: Helms
    given-names: Jessica
    affiliation: "FIVE@MGI, Washington University in St. Louis"
repository-code: "https://github.com/FIVE-MGI/SODA"
abstract: "SODA is a static browser viewer and a Python pipeline that turn the output of spatial biology instruments (multiplexed immunofluorescence, H&E, Visium and Visium HD, Xenium, CosMx, MERSCOPE, Stereo-seq, GeoMx DSP, single-cell RNA-seq, spatial AnnData, OME-Zarr and SpatialData) into folders of static files that can be hosted anywhere and opened with a link."
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - spatial proteomics
  - multiplexed immunofluorescence
  - image viewer
  - web browser
  - static hosting
